1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Nightingale is a shared care note for synthetic data.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:30,000
It is a trust system, not an autonomous medical system.
I use one patient workspace and an English interface.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The Top Card is designed for a fast glance.
It has no more than six source-linked items.

4
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Each card shows content, action, status, item kind, and risk.
Ranking priority is not a medical risk score.

5
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:28,000
This nurse entry is an AI-scribed suggestion. Open source takes me to the exact timeline entry.
The source panel names immutable version one and Python code-point offsets.
The highlight is the stored quote.

6
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:45,000
This optional prototype uses prerecorded synthetic audio and a mock timestamped transcript.
It demonstrates audio-to-summary provenance, but it does not claim live ASR or diarization.

7
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Now I switch to Staff.
There is no new-note composer, so I edit the existing Staff note.

8
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:25,000
I add an internal comment, choose Clinician A from the mention menu,
and submit it. The mention is stored as metadata.

9
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Resolve and Unresolve are explicit collaboration states.
Pin and Unpin provide feedback, but one click is not proof of learning.

10
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:05,000
History keeps full snapshots. Compare shows before and after.
Revert creates a new version and restores prior content.

11
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Longitudinal context combines current entries with older history.
It distinguishes Hot context, Warm index, and derived cold history.

12
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:32,000
The summary is labeled not the original record.
View original record scrolls to the canonical Patient summary.

13
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:47,000
The patient session is a different server-side projection.
Internal Glance, comments, tasks, and history controls are absent.

14
00:03:47,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Only patient-facing records and the patient Voice fixture appear.
The transcript is mock data and no source control is exposed.

15
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:10,000
The deployed service uses HTTPS and PostgreSQL, and this demo remains synthetic.

16
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:20,000
DeepSeek is only an optional redacted adapter.
This prototype is designed for a ten-second glance, not independently proven.
